      title: `mark>Section 1: Malignant Hyperthermia (MH) Deep Dive</mark>`,
      content: `Malignant hyperthermia (MH) is a devastating pharmacogenetic clinical syndrome that manifests primarily as a runaway hypermetabolic crisis in skeletal muscle following exposure to triggering volatile halogenated anesthetic agents or depolarizing neuromuscular blockers. It is inherited in an autosomal dominant pattern with variable penetrance.`
